## paper-search-mcp — MIT

<https://github.com/openags/paper-search-mcp>

The OpenAlex and Crossref support in
`src/just_module_creator/discovery.py` was **ported** from that project's
`paper_search_mcp/academic_platforms/openalex.py` and `crossref.py` under
`RM23`. What was taken is the API knowledge — endpoints, parameter names, and
the response shapes each service returns, including OpenAlex's inverted-index
abstract encoding. The implementation is written against this project's own
`ServiceGate`, `HttpService` and `LiteratureCandidate`.

Two things were changed rather than carried, both because this project has a
rule about them:

- **The contact address.** The original sends the literals
  `openags@example.com` (OpenAlex) and `paper-search@example.org` (Crossref) as
  the polite-pool contact. A fabricated address misattributes the traffic to a
  stranger, so ours resolves through `JMC_USER_EMAIL` →
  `JUST_DNA_CONTACT_EMAIL` → the project default.
- **The transport.** Every outbound request here goes through `net.py`, so the
  pacing and the shared NCBI budget cannot drift between clients.

No Sci-Hub code was taken, and the package is **not** a dependency of this
project.

